+# Daily Grind
+
+Run with Node.js 20+ using `npm start`. The server uses `PORT` (default 11222).
+No dependencies or build step are required.
+
+Newsletter submissions POST to `/api/newsletter` and are appended to
+`data/newsletter.jsonl`. Set `DATA_DIR` to a persistent, private directory in
+deployment. The server exposes only the homepage, stylesheet and signup script;
+subscriber files are never served. Serve production traffic over HTTPS through
+your reverse proxy, preserving the security response headers.
+
+The enforced Connection-Allowlist permits the response origin and
+https://images.unsplash.com only. Redirects and WebRTC remain blocked by default.
+A strict CSP restricts connections and form submissions to this server, images
+to this server and Unsplash, and scripts to the server-generated nonce.
+Browsers without Connection-Allowlist support receive the CSP fallback, which
+cannot cover every network channel (such as all navigations and WebRTC).
+
+Submission failures, including policy blocks, timeouts and server errors, show
+an accessible retry message without clearing the email. Native POST submission
+still works when JavaScript is unavailable.
+
+Browser security reports go to `/api/security-reports`; only receipt is logged,
+not report payloads or potentially sensitive URLs.
